{"text": "hospitable", "etymologies": [{"etymologyHTML": "<p>Borrowed from Middle French <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"frm\">hospitable</i>, formed from the root of Latin <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"la\">hospitare</i> with the suffix <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">-able</i>. Displaced native Old English <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"ang\">cuml\u012b\u00fee</i> (literally \u201cguest-gentle\u201d).\n</p>", "pos": [{"pos": "Adjective", "definitions": [{"definition": "cordial and generous towards guests\n", "quote": [], "relative": {"Synonym": ["guestfriendly"]}}, {"definition": "receptive and open-minded", "quote": [], "relative": {}}, {"definition": "favorable", "quote": [], "relative": {}}, {"definition": "favorable for life; livable; suitable for life.", "quote": [], "relative": {}}]}]}], "pronunciation": [["Received Pronunciation", "/h\u0252s\u02c8p\u026at\u0259bl\u0329/"], ["General American", "/h\u0251s\u02c8p\u026at\u0259bl\u0329/"]]}